course: dictionary
lesson: 14860
title: Rationed: shared out when there is not enough
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rationed comes from the word ration. When there is not enough of something for everyone, it is shared out in small, fixed amounts. That is what rationed means. The amount is limited, so each person can have only a little.
explain: «During the war, sugar and butter were rationed.» The clue is during the war, a time when things were scarce. So rationed means each person was allowed only a small, fixed amount. Try the swap: "During the war, sugar and butter were limited." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: You can also use rationed for yourself. «I rationed my sweets so they would last all week.» Here it means you used them carefully, in small amounts, so they did not run out. The sentence tells you why: so they would last.
fact: Ration means a fixed, limited amount of something given to each person.
fact: «Rationed» means limited to a fixed amount, because there is not enough to go round.
fact: «Rationed» can also mean used carefully in small amounts to make it last.
fact: In Britain during the Second World War, food such as sugar, butter and meat was rationed, and people used ration books to get it.
fact: In maths, rationing means sharing a fixed amount equally, so each person gets the same share.
exercise: «During the war, sugar and butter were rationed.» What does rationed mean? | Thrown away after every meal | Sold at a much higher price | Made into cakes for everyone | *Limited to a small, fixed amount each
exercise: Maya «rationed her crisps» so they would last all week. What does rationed mean here? | Gave them away to her friends | Ate them all at once | Lost them in the park | *Used carefully in small amounts
exercise: «Each family could buy only one egg a week, because eggs were rationed.» Why were eggs rationed? | Everyone wanted to be a chicken | Eggs were too big to fit in the shops | Eggs were free to take | *There was not enough for everyone
test: «In the drought, the village's water was rationed.» Why was the water rationed? | Because the water tasted nice | Because it was raining every day | Because the village had too much water | *Because there was not enough water for everyone
test: The phrase «rationed food» means what? | Food cooked in a hurry | Food brought from far away | *Food given out in fixed, limited amounts | Food that tastes bad
exam: Which sentence uses rationed to mean used carefully so it lasts? | My sweets came in a big box | I ate all my sweets in one go | *I rationed my sweets so they lasted all week | I gave my sweets to the school fair
